tinytime is an independent C99 implementation of standard proleptic Gregorian,
Julian-date and astronomical time-offset arithmetic. TinyNadir contributions
are MIT licensed; no ERFA/SOFA or Vallado implementation source is included.

Independent numerical validation used pyerfa 2.0.1.5 (ERFA/SOFA cal2jd/dtdb)
and NumPy 2.5.4. The TT-to-TDB function is the documented geocentric two-term
approximation, not the complete ERFA dtdb model. See README.md for supported
scales, ranges, comparison errors and the uniform-day/leap-second contract.
Reference packages/generators/raw results remain in ignored .validation/;
only numeric reference fixtures are retained in tests/data/.

References: https://www.iausofa.org/current-software
            https://github.com/liberfa/erfa
